    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. His matchup against the right-handed Matthews is optimal, as the combination of an favorable opposing xERA and a significant boost from dynamic platoon splits makes him a lock for a massive output. **Drake Baldwin** (68.63) also presents an elite start, taking advantage of a favorable 4.62 xERA and a high-leverage leadoff spot. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (64.08) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.03) are providing the high-floor stability required to anchor our offensive production, with the latter benefiting from a strong platoon advantage despite the respectable xERA of Ranger Suarez.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today\u2019s lineup was the exclusion of **Wade Meckler** (48.50), who missed the final cut by a narrow margin. While **Wade Meckler** offered potential utility against Cal Quantrill, his lower-tier batting order projection and lack of elite speed compared to our active options pushed him to the bench in favor of prioritizing high-upside speed threats. We are also keeping a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Andy Pages**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Dominic Smith**. The most notable risk is the dynamic platoon situation for **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose score was dragged down by a -15% adjustment, necessitating close monitoring of the official card to ensure he isn't squeezed out of a high-leverage spot. We remain cautious regarding **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined, and continue to evaluate **Heliot Ramos** as a high-potential pinch-hit option should weather or last-minute defensive adjustments disrupt our starting core.",
